ke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:4 3"/><text x="294" y="246" font-size="14" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8)">13</text></svg>', 'A 2 × 2 block of voxels with readings: top row 10, bottom row 14, left column 9, right column 15, and 13 along the diagonal from top-left to bottom-right.'),
('0ef10fc4-e9e3-57b0-9f95-a2d6728a46d0', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', 'b4831698-a4b4-443d-99d1-518973eaa5a7', 'a-level', '30.4', '9702 coursebook 30.4 · Computerised axial tomography', 28, 28, 'What mainly limits the spatial resolution of a CT image?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'The size of the voxels', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Detail smaller than a voxel is averaged out. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: voxel size. C1: averaging within voxel. A1: C (The size of the voxels).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('8c663aab-cf11-5a67-a2aa-604dc5b3b435', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', 'b4831698-a4b4-443d-99d1-518973eaa5a7', 'a-level', '30.4', '9702 coursebook 30.4 · Computerised axial tomography', 29, 29, 'A CT voxel is 0.50 mm × 0.50 mm × 1.0 mm. Calculate its volume in mm³.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.25', 'mm³', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'V = 0.50 × 0.50 × 1.0 = 0.25 mm³. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: product. C1: units. A1: V = 0.25 mm³.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('bc983182-6b89-544e-8422-a6ac97bc990c', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', 'b4831698-a4b4-443d-99d1-518973eaa5a7', 'a-level', '30.4', '9702 coursebook 30.4 · Computerised axial tomography', 30, 30, 'A region 300 mm × 300 mm × 150 mm is imaged with voxels 0.50 mm × 0.50 mm × 1.0 mm. How many voxels is that?', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '5.4e7', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'N = (300 ÷ 0.50) × (300 ÷ 0.50) × (150 ÷ 1.0) = 5.4 × 10⁷. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: voxels along each side. C1: product. A1: N = 5.4 × 10⁷.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('18d671fa-d7e8-593c-8d44-48b27782a446', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', 'b4831698-a4b4-443d-99d1-518973eaa5a7', 'a-level', '30.4', '9702 coursebook 30.4 · Computerised axial tomography', 31, 31, 'Why must a patient keep still during a CT scan?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'The image is reconstructed from many projections assumed to be of the same object; movement blurs it', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Inconsistent projections produce artefacts. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: projections combined. C1: movement causes blur or artefacts. A1: A (The image is reconstructed from many projections assumed to be of the same object; movement blurs it).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('195b9fdb-f9d7-5ace-9946-dccf582b3975', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', 'b4831698-a4b4-443d-99d1-518973eaa5a7', 'a-level', '30.4', '9702 coursebook 30.4 · Computerised axial tomography', 32, 32, 'A CT gantry makes one rotation every 0.40 s. Calculate its angular speed.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '15.71', 'rad s⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'ω = 2π ÷ 0.40 = 15.7 rad s⁻¹. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: ω = 2π/T. C1: value. A1: ω = 15.7 rad s⁻¹.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('031465a6-acc0-535d-a7bd-3f868ba719e2', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', 'b4831698-a4b4-443d-99d1-518973eaa5a7', 'a-level', '30.4', '9702 coursebook 30.4 · Computerised axial tomography', 33, 33, 'A CT detector arc has 900 elements, each recording 1000 readings per 0.50 s rotation. How many readings are recorded per second?', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.8e6', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Readings = 900 × 1000 ÷ 0.50 = 1.8 × 10⁶. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: per rotation. C1: per second. A1: readings = 1.8 × 10⁶.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('ede710cf-f758-5573-b4b6-164d51d2d358', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', 'b4831698-a4b4-443d-99d1-518973eaa5a7', 'a-level', '30.4', '9702 coursebook 30.4 · Computerised axial tomography', 34, 34, 'Why is an iodine contrast agent sometimes injected before a CT scan?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'It raises the attenuation of blood, making vessels and some organs stand out', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'High-Z iodine increases μ where it collects. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: increases μ. C1: improves contrast. A1: D (It raises the attenuation of blood, making vessels and some organs stand out).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('800625f9-4479-5d1b-ac08-076e0c1dc9ee', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', 'b4831698-a4b4-443d-99d1-518973eaa5a7', 'a-level', '30.4', '9702 coursebook 30.4 · Computerised axial tomography', 35, 35, 'A path through a patient crosses 4 voxels, and the total attenuation along it is 2.4. What is the mean attenuation per voxel?', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.6', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Mean = 2.4 ÷ 4 = 0.60. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: total ÷ number. C1: value. A1: mean = 0.60.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('aed84718-c1d0-587d-b778-e870749849cd', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', 'b4831698-a4b4-443d-99d1-518973eaa5a7', 'a-level', '30.4', '9702 coursebook 30.4 · Computerised axial tomography', 36, 36, 'What does the computer in a CT scanner calculate from the detector readings?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'The attenuation of each voxel in the slice', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Back-projection solves for individual voxel values. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: voxel attenuation. C1: from many projections. A1: B (The attenuation of each voxel in the slice).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('1b7589b3-f8c0-570f-8d81-5be170590073', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', 'b4831698-a4b4-443d-99d1-518973eaa5a7', 'a-level', '30.4', '9702 coursebook 30.4 · Computerised axial tomography', 37, 37, 'In a helical CT scan the table moves 20 mm per rotation and the beam is 10 mm wide. Calculate the pitch (table movement per rotation ÷ beam width).', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '2', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Pitch = 20 ÷ 10 = 2.0. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: ratio. C1: value. A1: pitch = 2.0.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('f99d99f2-7db2-51fd-afcc-7252155673ad', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', 'b4831698-a4b4-443d-99d1-518973eaa5a7', 'a-level', '30.4', '9702 coursebook 30.4 · Computerised axial tomography', 38, 38, 'A scan covers 400 mm of a patient at a table speed of 80 mm s⁻¹. Calculate the scan time.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '5', 's', false, NULL, false, NULL, 't = 400 ÷ 80 = 5.0 s. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: t = d/v. C1: value. A1: t = 5.0 s.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('da61bf7f-6818-5ea1-8940-4ee778df44c8', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', 'b4831698-a4b4-443d-99d1-518973eaa5a7', 'a-level', '30.4', '9702 coursebook 30.4 · Computerised axial tomography', 39, 39, 'Why does a CT scanner use a fan-shaped beam and an arc of detectors?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'So that many paths through the slice are measured at once for each angle', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Each detector records one path. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: many paths per projection. C1: faster data collection. A1: C (So that many paths through the slice are measured at once for each angle).', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 360 320" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgd3bdded9-t fgd3bdded9-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgd3bdded9-t">CT scanner</title><desc id="fgd3bdded9-d">End-on view of a CT scanner: the X-ray tube and an opposite arc of detectors rotate together round the patient; a fan-shaped beam crosses the slice.</desc><circle cx="180" cy="160" r="120" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:5 4"/><circle cx="180" cy="160" r="48" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="180" y="160" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">patient</text><rect x="160" y="28" width="40" height="24" rx="4" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="208" y="28" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309)">X-ray tube</text><rect x="108.9" y="255.5" width="8" height="8" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="116" y="259.9" width="8" height="8" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="123.4" y="263.9" width="8" height="8" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="131" y="267.3" width="8" height="8" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="138.9" y="270.1" width="8" height="8" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="147" y="272.4" width="8" height="8" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="155.2" y="274.2" width="8" height="8" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="163.5" y="275.3" width="8" height="8" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="171.8" y="275.9" width="8" height="8" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="180.2" y="275.9" width="8" height="8" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="188.5" y="275.3" width="8" height="8" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="196.8" y="274.2" width="8" height="8" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="205" y="272.4" width="8" height="8" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="213.1" y="270.1" width="8" height="8" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="221" y="267.3" width="8" height="8" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="228.6" y="263.9" width="8" height="8" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="236" y="259.9" width="8" height="8" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="243.1" y="255.5" width="8" height="8" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="180" y1="52" x2="112.9" y2="255.5" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="180" y1="52" x2="180" y2="276" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="180" y1="52" x2="247.1" y2="255.5" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="250" y="276" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">detector arc</text><path d="M114,45.7 A132,132 0 0,0 56,114.9" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="56,114.9 55.3,106.9 61.6,109.2" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/></svg>', 'End-on view of a CT scanner: the X-ray tube and an opposite arc of detectors rotate together round the patient; a fan-shaped beam crosses the slice.'),
('e4eae288-dfda-5f6c-b5a4-9957555c0a1e', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', 'b4831698-a4b4-443d-99d1-518973eaa5a7', 'a-level', '30.4', '9702 coursebook 30.4 · Computerised axial tomography', 40, 40, 'A 64-slice scanner covers 40 mm along the patient in each rotation. Calculate the slice thickness in mm.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.625 mm', 'mm', false, NULL, false, NULL, 't = 40 ÷ 64 = 0.625 mm. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: width ÷ slices. C1: value. A1: t = 0.625 mm.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('bf2d42f0-274d-5435-b833-0bbfee8d28b5', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', 'b4831698-a4b4-443d-99d1-518973eaa5a7', 'a-level', '30.4', '9702 coursebook 30.4 · Computerised axial tomography', 41, 41, 'The diagram shows a 2 × 2 block of voxels with top row 12, bottom row 8, left column 11 and right column 9. The diagonal through the top-left and bottom-right voxels reads 10. (a) Write the voxel values in terms of the top-left value a. (b) Find a. (c) Find the value of the bottom-left voxel. Give only the answer to (c).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '4.5', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) Top-right 12 − a, bottom-left 11 − a, bottom-right 10 − a. (b) Bottom row: (11 − a) + (10 − a) = 8, so a = (21 − 8) ÷ 2 = 6.5. (c) Bottom-left = 11 − 6.5 = 4.5. Mark scheme (5 marks). B1: expressions. M1: use the bottom-row sum. C1: a. C1: value. A1: value = 4.5.', 5, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 360 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgbb6d5d05-t fgbb6d5d05-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgbb6d5d05-t">Reconstructing a block</title><desc id="fgbb6d5d05-d">A 2 × 2 block of voxels with readings: top row 12, bottom row 8, left column 11, right column 9, and 10 along the diagonal from top-left to bottom-right.</desc><rect x="110" y="60" width="80" height="80" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="150" y="100" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">a</text><rect x="190" y="60" width="80" height="80" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="110" y="140" width="80" height="80" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="150" y="180" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">?</text><rect x="190" y="140" width="80" height="80" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="30" y1="100" x2="99.8" y2="100" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="104,100 98.6,102.5 98.6,97.5" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke:none"/><line x1="274" y1="100" x2="300" y2="100" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="306" y="100" font-size="14" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309)">12</text><line x1="30" y1="180" x2="99.8" y2="180" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="104,180 98.6,182.5 98.6,177.5" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke:none"/><line x1="274" y1="180" x2="300" y2="180" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="306" y="180" font-size="14" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309)">8</text><line x1="150" y1="18" x2="150" y2="49.8" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="150,54 147.5,48.6 152.5,48.6" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke:none"/><text x="150" y="242" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309)">11</text><line x1="230" y1="18" x2="230" y2="49.8" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="230,54 227.5,48.6 232.5,48.6" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke:none"/><text x="230" y="242" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309)">9</text><line x1="86" y1="36" x2="288" y2="238" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:4 3"/><text x="294" y="246" font-size="14" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8)">10</text></svg>', 'A 2 × 2 block of voxels with readings: top row 12, bottom row 8, left column 11, right column 9, and 10 along the diagonal from top-left to bottom-right.'),
('50c4e885-d642-5c36-9ce6-8f0050082878', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', 'b4831698-a4b4-443d-99d1-518973eaa5a7', 'a-level', '30.4', '9702 coursebook 30.4 · Computerised axial tomography', 42, 42, 'In a 2 × 2 block, top row 16, bottom row 6, left column 13 and right column 9; the diagonal through top-left and bottom-right reads 11. (a) Find all four voxel values. (b) Identify which voxel is most likely bone. (c) Give the value of that voxel.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '9', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) With top-left a: bottom-right 11 − a, bottom-left 13 − a. Bottom row: (13 − a) + (11 − a) = 6, so a = (24 − 6) ÷ 2 = 9; top-right = 16 − 9 = 7, bottom-left = 4, bottom-right = 2. (b) The top-left voxel has the highest attenuation. (c) Its value is 9. Mark scheme (6 marks). M1: method. C1: a. C1: other values. B1: bone has highest attenuation. C1: value. A1: value = 9.', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 360 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg772c20cf-t fg772c20cf-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg772c20cf-t">Finding the bone voxel</title><desc id="fg772c20cf-d">A 2 × 2 block of voxels with readings: top row 16, bottom row 6, left column 13, right column 9, and 11 along the diagonal from top-left to bottom-right.</desc><rect x="110" y="60" width="80" height="80" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="190" y="60" width="80" height="80" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="110" y="140" width="80" height="80" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="190" y="140" width="80" height="80" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="30" y1="100" x2="99.8" y2="100" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="104,100 98.6,102.5 98.6,97.5" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke:none"/><line x1="274" y1="100" x2="300" y2="100" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="306" y="100" font-size="14" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309)">16</text><line x1="30" y1="180" x2="99.8" y2="180" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="104,180 98.6,182.5 98.6,177.5" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke:none"/><line x1="274" y1="180" x2="300" y2="180" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="306" y="180" font-size="14" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309)">6</text><line x1="150" y1="18" x2="150" y2="49.8" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="150,54 147.5,48.6 152.5,48.6" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke:none"/><text x="150" y="242" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309)">13</text><line x1="230" y1="18" x2="230" y2="49.8" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="230,54 227.5,48.6 232.5,48.6" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke:none"/><text x="230" y="242" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309)">9</text><line x1="86" y1="36" x2="288" y2="238" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:4 3"/><text x="294" y="246" font-size="14" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8)">11</text></svg>', 'A 2 × 2 block of voxels with readings: top row 16, bottom row 6, left column 13, right column 9, and 11 along the diagonal from top-left to bottom-right.'),
('f11a05bf-eed5-501d-b789-fab2305b4d8a', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', 'b4831698-a4b4-443d-99d1-518973eaa5a7', 'a-level', '30.4', '9702 coursebook 30.4 · Computerised axial tomography', 43, 43, 'A CT scan has 200 slices, each 512 × 512 pixels stored as 2 bytes. (a) Calculate the bytes per slice. (b) Calculate the total data in MB (1 MB = 10⁶ bytes).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '104.9', 'MB', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) 512 × 512 × 2 = 524 288 bytes. (b) 524 288 × 200 ÷ 10⁶ = 105 MB. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: per slice. M1: × slices. C1: ÷ 10⁶. C1: value. A1: size = 105 MB.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('ed1d12e8-a109-591a-9afe-201c8e303ac9', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', 'b4831698-a4b4-443d-99d1-518973eaa5a7', 'a-level', '30.4', '9702 coursebook 30.4 · Computerised axial tomography', 44, 44, 'A helical CT scanner rotates once every 0.50 s with a beam width of 40 mm and a pitch of 1.5. (a) Calculate the table movement per rotation. (b) Calculate the table speed. (c) Calculate the time to scan 600 mm. Give only the answer to (c).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '5', 's', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) 1.5 × 40 = 60 mm. (b) 60 ÷ 0.50 = 120 mm s⁻¹. (c) t = 600 ÷ 120 = 5.0 s. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: pitch × width. C1: per rotation. C1: speed. M1: t = d/v. C1: value. A1: t = 5.0 s.', 6, NULL, NULL),
('343b94e0-3a55-5683-8c1f-031dbf7b7f82', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', 'b4831698-a4b4-443d-99d1-518973eaa5a7', 'a-level', '30.4', '9702 coursebook 30.4 · Computerised axial tomography', 45, 45, 'A beam path crosses 10 voxels, each 1.0 cm long: 9 are soft tissue (μ = 0.20 cm⁻¹) and one is bone (μ = 0.50 cm⁻¹). (a) Calculate the total μx. (b) Calculate the fraction of the beam transmitted.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.1003', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) μx = 9 × 0.20 × 1.0 + 0.50 × 1.0 = 2.3. (b) e^(−2.3) = 0.100. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: tissue sum. C1: add bone. M1: e^(−Σμx). C1: value. A1: fraction = 0.100.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('8490078c-39c2-50e9-a958-4db2dbfd106d', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', 'b4831698-a4b4-443d-99d1-518973eaa5a7', 'a-level', '30.4', '9702 coursebook 30.4 · Computerised axial tomography', 46, 46, 'A CT scan deposits a dose of 10 mGy in a 5.0 kg region of the body (1 Gy = 1 J kg⁻¹). (a) Calculate the energy absorbed, in mJ. (b) Explain why the risk is still considered acceptable for a diagnosis.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '50 mJ', 'mJ', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) E = 10 × 10⁻³ × 5.0 = 0.050 J. In mJ: 0.050 × 10³ = 50. (b) The diagnostic benefit outweighs the small extra cancer risk. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: Gy as J kg⁻¹. M1: E = D × m. C1: value. C1: J to mJ. B1: benefit vs risk. A1: E = 50 mJ.', 6, NULL, NULL),
('7a76ea12-ef08-5b47-9378-952da0d025e7', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', 'b4831698-a4b4-443d-99d1-518973eaa5a7', 'a-level', '30.4', '9702 coursebook 30.4 · Computerised axial tomography', 47, 47, 'A CT scanner records 1000 projections per rotation with 800 detector elements, each reading stored as 2 bytes. (a) Calculate the number of readings per rotation. (b) Calculate the data per rotation, in MB (1 MB = 10⁶ bytes).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.6', 'MB', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) 1000 × 800 = 8.0 × 10⁵. (b) 8.0 × 10⁵ × 2 ÷ 10⁶ = 1.6 MB. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: readings. C1: bytes. M1: ÷ 10⁶. C1: value. A1: size = 1.6 MB.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('5ac59c4e-3573-5f8f-a035-fe7d574e8fba', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', 'b4831698-a4b4-443d-99d1-518973eaa5a7', 'a-level', '30.4', '9702 coursebook 30.4 · Computerised axial tomography', 48, 48, 'A slice is 400 mm across and imaged as 512 × 512 pixels; the slice is 1.0 mm thick. (a) Calculate the pixel width. (b) Calculate the voxel volume in mm³. (c) A tumour 2.0 mm across is imaged. How many voxels wide is it? Give only the answer to (b).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.6104', 'mm³', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) 400 ÷ 512 = 0.7812 mm. (b) V = (0.7812)² × 1.0 = 0.610 mm³. (c) 2.0 ÷ 0.7812 ≈ 2.6 voxels. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: pixel width. M1: volume = w² × t. C1: substitution. C1: value. C1: tumour width in voxels. A1: V = 0.610 mm³.', 6, NULL, NULL),
('1316fa17-0b46-5090-9f5e-74b7a3373688', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', 'b4831698-a4b4-443d-99d1-518973eaa5a7', 'a-level', '30.4', '9702 coursebook 30.4 · Computerised axial tomography', 49, 49, 'A 2 × 2 voxel block has these readings: top row 5.0, bottom row 3.0, left column 4.5, right column 3.5, and diagonal (top-left + bottom-right) 4.0. (a) Find the top-left value. (b) Find the top-right value. Give only the answer to (b).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '2.25', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) Bottom-left = 4.5 − a, bottom-right = 4.0 − a, so (4.5 − a) + (4.0 − a) = 3.0, a = (8.5 − 3.0) ÷ 2 = 2.75. (b) Top-right = 5.0 − 2.75 = 2.25. Mark scheme (5 marks). M1: express in a. C1: equation. C1: a. C1: top-right. A1: value = 2.25.', 5, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 360 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgbf30e8e8-t fgbf30e8e8-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgbf30e8e8-t">Reconstructing a block</title><desc id="fgbf30e8e8-d">A 2 × 2 block of voxels with readings: top row 5.0, bottom row 3.0, left column 4.5, right column 3.5, and 4.0 along the diagonal from top-left to bottom-right.</desc><rect x="110" y="60" width="80" height="80" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="150" y="100" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">a</text><rect x="190" y="60" width="80" height="80" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="230" y="100" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">?</text><rect x="110" y="140" width="80" height="80" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="190" y="140" width="80" height="80" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="30" y1="100" x2="99.8" y2="100" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="104,100 98.6,102.5 98.6,97.5" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke:none"/><line x1="274" y1="100" x2="300" y2="100" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="306" y="100" font-size="14" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309)">5.0</text><line x1="30" y1="180" x2="99.8" y2="180" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="104,180 98.6,182.5 98.6,177.5" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke:none"/><line x1="274" y1="180" x2="300" y2="180" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="306" y="180" font-size="14" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309)">3.0</text><line x1="150" y1="18" x2="150" y2="49.8" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="150,54 147.5,48.6 152.5,48.6" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke:none"/><text x="150" y="242" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309)">4.5</text><line x1="230" y1="18" x2="230" y2="49.8" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="230,54 227.5,48.6 232.5,48.6" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke:none"/><text x="230" y="242" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309)">3.5</text><line x1="86" y1="36" x2="288" y2="238" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:4 3"/><text x="294" y="246" font-size="14" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8)">4.0</text></svg>', 'A 2 × 2 block of voxels with readings: top row 5.0, bottom row 3.0, left column 4.5, right column 3.5, and 4.0 along the diagonal from top-left to bottom-right.'),
('5bd8b167-9313-5283-b44b-c22ad3fd6b00', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', 'b4831698-a4b4-443d-99d1-518973eaa5a7', 'a-level', '30.4', '9702 coursebook 30.4 · Computerised axial tomography', 50, 50, 'A CT examination gives an effective dose of 6.0 mSv, while natural background gives about 2.4 mSv per year. (a) Calculate the scan dose in years of background. (b) Calculate the dose from 15 chest radiographs of 0.020 mSv each, and compare. Give only the answer to (a), in years.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '2.5', 'years', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) 6.0 ÷ 2.4 = 2.5 years. (b) 15 × 0.020 = 0.30 mSv, far less than one CT scan. Mark scheme (6 marks). M1: ratio. C1: value. C1: radiograph total. B1: comparison. B1: units consistent. A1: equivalent = 2.5 years.', 6, NULL, NULL)
